-- title:
--   Raised local component at level Nq² with U_q=0
-- statement:
--   Fix non-zero naturals $N$ and $q$ with $q$ prime and $q\nmid N$, together with three hypotheses [`CohCarrier.LevelLE`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L330) for the pair of levels $N\mid Nq^2$ with full subgroups $\top$ and degeneracy parameters $d=1$, $q$, $q^2$ (each asserting $N\mid Nq^2$, $d\mid q^2$, and that reduction carries $\top$ into $\top$). Fix a set of naturals $S$ with $q\in S$ and a Noetherian local ring $\mathcal O$ that is complete for its maximal ideal, with residue field $k$. For a level $M$, $H^1(M,\top,\mathcal O)$ is the additive homomorphisms from $\Gamma_0(M)$ (written additively) to $\mathcal O$, and [`CohCarrier.Gen M S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) has generators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid M$), $U_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\mid M$) and $\langle d\rangle$ for $d\in(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$, sent by [`CohCarrier.opFamily`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) to the transfer-plus-conjugation operator `heckeTL` at $\ell$, respectively to the diamond operator. Assume these operators commute pairwise at levels $N$ (hypothesis `hcomm`) and $Nq^2$ (`hcomm'`). Given eigensystems $\bar\theta$ on `Gen N S` and $\bar\theta'$ on `Gen (N*q^2) S` with values in $k$, assume $\bar\theta'(T_\ell)=\bar\theta(T_\ell)$ for $\ell\nmid Nq^2$, $\bar\theta'(U_\ell)=\bar\theta(U_\ell)$ for primes $\ell\mid N$, $\bar\theta'(U_q)=0$, and $\bar\theta'(\langle d\rangle)=1$ for all $d$. Assume further: an idempotent splitting `Sp` of the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal O}H^1(N,\top,\mathcal O)$ generated by the operators attached to $\bar\theta$'s generators (a family of complete orthogonal idempotents indexed by the maximal ideals), an index $i_0$, and an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\pi_k$ from the corner ring $e_{i_0}\mathbb T e_{i_0}$ to $k$ with $\pi_k(e_{i_0}\,\mathrm{op}(g)\,e_{i_0})=\bar\theta(g)$ for every generator $g$; and that the combination $q\,\iota_1^{*}-\iota_q^{*}\circ T_q+\iota_{q^2}^{*}$ is injective on the corner submodule $e_{i_0}H^1(N,\top,\mathcal O)$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an idempotent splitting `Sp'` of the corresponding subalgebra at level $Nq^2$, an index $i_0'$, and an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\pi_{k}'$ on the corner ring at $i_0'$ with $\pi_k'(e_{i_0'}\,\mathrm{op}(g)\,e_{i_0'})=\bar\theta'(g)$ for every generator $g$ of `Gen (N*q^2) S`.
--
--   This is the existence of the raised local component in a single level-raising step at a prime $q\nmid N$: the residual eigensystem at level $N$, with $U_q$ set to zero at level $Nq^2$, is realised by a maximal ideal of the Hecke algebra of level $Nq^2$, the injectivity hypothesis on $q\,\iota_1^{*}-\iota_q^{*}T_q+\iota_{q^2}^{*}$ supplying non-vanishing of the image of the corner module under the degeneracy combination. It feeds the construction of corner realisations at raised level used in the modularity-lifting argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CohCarrier_exists_idempotentSplitting_algHom_apply_toCornerRing_eq_level_mul_sq_of_prime.lean

